Adaptations made for JayNet (2026-08):

* SKILL.md — shortened the frontmatter `description` (it rides in every
  system prompt via the skill catalog); replaced the "Optional: the
  controller" section with "The machinery in this harness", mapping the
  upstream `jspace.py` ledger controller onto JayNet features (`todos`
  tool, workspace files via `fs.*`, `context.pin`, and the `run.badge`
  tool); added the "Show the pass" gate rule; rewrote the
  resume-after-gap and ledger-register wording accordingly.
* modules/shorthand.md — one line: "Ledger-controller arguments" reworded
  to "Ledger lines" (no ledger controller ships here).
* scripts/workspace-ledger.md — replaced the `jspace.py note` creation
  hint with plain file creation and self-numbered entries.
* scripts/jspace.py and scripts/verify_suite.py are NOT shipped: their
  ledger-recording role is covered by the harness mapping above.

The premise, gate, the original nine modules, and all three references
are otherwise verbatim from V3.6.

Additions from SV1 (2026-10 — upstream renamed the repository to
"J-Space-Cognition-Suite"; the URL above redirects):

* modules/epistemics.md, modules/cyber.md — vendored from SV1 with
  these adaptations: the upstream `security add`/`security resolve`
  controller commands are mapped to workspace evidence files
  (`.jspace/security/<slug>.md` via `fs.write`); cross-references to
  unvendored SV1 files (orchestration.md, repository.md,
  controller.md, engineering-evidence.md, problem-model.md) are mapped
  to harness equivalents (`council.vote` or a delegated review for
  independent perspectives, `code.symbols`/`fs.*` for source tracing,
  `references/j-space-science.md` for the evidence base,
  `scripts/workspace-ledger.md` for the ledger format). Otherwise
  verbatim from SV1.
* SKILL.md — two routing-table rows for the new modules; the
  frontmatter `description` gained "separating evidence from
  inference, authorized security analysis".

SV1's `control.py`, `host_bridge.py`, and the remaining SV1 modules
(orchestration, repository) are NOT shipped: their gate/map/agent
roles are covered natively by the harness (verify gates, delegation
review, todos, context management).
